Use the platform id_t for waitid when observing shell snapshot captures.

Tokio returns a child PID as u32, but Solaris declares waitid's PID argument
as a signed id_t. Cast the OS-created child PID to the libc API's native type;
its value is already a valid process ID. Preserve WNOWAIT and process-group
cleanup semantics. On platforms with an unsigned id_t this is unchanged.

diff --git a/codex-rs/exec-server/src/shell_snapshot_process.rs b/codex-rs/exec-server/src/shell_snapshot_process.rs
--- a/codex-rs/exec-server/src/shell_snapshot_process.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/exec-server/src/shell_snapshot_process.rs
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ impl SnapshotCapture {
                 if unsafe {
                     libc::waitid(
                         libc::P_PID,
-                        pid,
+                        pid as libc::id_t,
                         info.as_mut_ptr(),
                         libc::WEXITED | libc::WNOHANG | libc::WNOWAIT,
                     )
